From: Thomas Gleixner <tglx@linutronix.de>
Subject: [PATCH] rseq: Add time slice extension support with stats and whitelist

This patch adds the RSEQ time slice extension feature which allows
user-space memory allocators (like TCMalloc, jemalloc) to request a
brief scheduling delay when they're in the middle of a critical section,
avoiding expensive aborts.

Key features:
- New syscall rseq_slice_yield (471) for cooperative yielding
- New prctl PR_RSEQ_SLICE_EXTENSION for enable/disable
- Configurable slice extension time via sysctl
- Statistics tracking via /sys/kernel/debug/rseq/stats
- Per-syscall abort tracking (top 20 syscalls)
- Syscall whitelist to preserve grants through fast syscalls:
  rt_sigprocmask, getrusage, getpid, gettid, clock_gettime, gettimeofday, sched_yield

Based on upstream commits from Thomas Gleixner's RSEQ v6 patchset.
Stats and whitelist additions by BobZKernel.

Signed-off-by: Thomas Gleixner <tglx@linutronix.de>
Signed-off-by: Bob <bob@localhost>
---
